## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/equalize.html
- Summary (EN): The Equalize node rescales or repositions a layer's colors so they fit a desired range. It is most useful when the input's range is unknown and must be mapped onto a specific one.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Equalize recale les couleurs d'une couche dans une plage voulue, utile quand la plage d'origine est inconnue.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: layer or VDB to equalize", "active: optional layer or VDB whose pixels define the range used for equalization; pixels above 0.5 are considered", "mask: optional per-pixel mask scaling the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by the source", "Mask: how much of the equalized value is mixed into the original; default 1 uses only the new value; also selects affected channels", "Toggle RGB and Red, Green, Blue, Alpha: enable or disable each channel's effect", "Equalize By: Stretch (min and max to Black and White), Move Minimum to Black, Move Maximum to White, Move Average to Target Average, Scale to Maximum Length", "Fit Method: shift or scale to reach a goal value; ignored by Stretch and Scale to Maximum Length", "Luminance Type: brightness formula such as SGI, NTSC or HDTV luminance, or average, max or min channel, magnitude, HSV hue, saturation or value, or single-channel extraction", "Black and White: target values, usually 0 and 1", "Target Average: goal average when Equalize By is Move Average to Value"]

- Caveats: ["The range is computed from the input, so a frame with unusually extreme values can cause sudden unwanted changes in a procedural setup", "The page recommends a Remap COP with a fixed range instead, which is also faster because it skips the range computation"]

